  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "Independent hand-labeled diagnostic corpus for default prefix-regex versus native complete-syllable phrase retrieval.",
  "labeling_policy": [
    "Gold positives were assigned from human-declared query intent and the displayed whitespace-separated syllables, not from regex, native query outputs, dictionary parsing, or measured result sets.",
    "Every case exhaustively labels all 50 rows: negative_ids is the mechanical complement of its manually specified positive_ids.",
    "Full intent requires complete syllables; initials intent requires adjacent first-letter positions; autocomplete intent keeps earlier syllables complete and broadens only the final prefix.",
    "Relevant term and phrase occurrences may appear anywhere inside longer text. This fixture does not impose whole-field equality.",
    "Slope zero requires adjacency and order. The single distinct-token slope-one case admits one intervening token, but not a reversed adjacent pair; repeated-term tests use slope zero.",
    "Normalization cases use complete-syllable intent and are a separate input-acceptance group. Unsupported tone or umlaut inputs must not be presented as a recall loss caused by exact matching.",
    "Names are illustrative readable snippets, including synthetic names and positional controls, rather than claims that every name is a registered real-world place or person.",
    "This deliberately adversarial small corpus measures diagnostic behavior, not a population estimate of production error or recall rates."
  ],
